data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":243,"item_id":"fc_0bfe6e1fa8f24ccf016adb3ce80b6881918a2e916151a3d5f4","output_index":0,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_candidate\\\":25,\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/4/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"At time r set g_j=u_t·u_{x_j}. Smoothness and compact support give continuous compactly supported derivatives, so they are integrable by M001. On each coordinate line integrate by parts with M007, taking v=1; the boundary values of g_j vanish, so the integral of ∂_j g_j on that line is zero. M003 applies to the product-integrable coordinate-permuted derivative, giving ∫∂_j g_j=0. Expanding the product derivative yields ∫u_{x_j}·∂_j u_t=−∫u_t·u_{x_jx_j}. Summing over j and differentiating the finite Frobenius energy sum gives ∫e_t=2∫u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu). The already established identity E′(r)=∫e_t(x,r)dx therefore gives E′(r)=2∫u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu).\\\"}]}\"}"}

